meta {
  name: List Zip Markets
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/platform/mailer-zip-markets?q=9999&page=1&pageSize=25
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  q: 9999
  page: 1
  pageSize: 25
  ~agencyId: 
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{platformAccessToken}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 200) {
    const row = res.getBody().items.find((r) => r.zip5 === "99998");
    if (row) bru.setVar("zipMarketId", row.id);
    // 99999 is what `Platform Mailer Campaigns/Patch Zip Resolutions` wrote
    // back mid-run. Captured so the next request can remove it and leave the
    // table as this run found it — see that request's docs.
    const resolved = res.getBody().items.find((r) => r.zip5 === "99999");
    bru.setVar("campaignZipMarketId", resolved ? resolved.id : "missing");
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("finds the row by ZIP prefix", function () {
    const row = res.getBody().items.find((r) => r.zip5 === "99998");
    expect(row, "the upserted row is listed").to.not.equal(undefined);
    expect(row.market).to.equal("Bruno Test Market");
    // `null` is a value here, not an absence — the platform-global scope.
    expect(row.agencyId).to.equal(null);
  });

  test("carries the resolution the campaign preview wrote back", function () {
    // `Platform Mailer Campaigns/Patch Zip Resolutions` resolves 99999 → Tulsa
    // mid-run, and the answer is persisted here so the next campaign starts
    // with it. That is the whole of ApexReports' resolver flow.
    const row = res.getBody().items.find((r) => r.zip5 === "99999");
    if (row) {
      expect(row.market).to.equal("Tulsa");
      expect(row.source).to.equal("preview");
    }
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /platform/mailer-zip-markets — the ZIP → market table

  - **Module:** none (`@SkipModule()`)
  - **Permission:** `platform:mailers:read`
  - **Data scope:** none (`@SkipTenant()`, `@SkipBranch()`)

  ## Query
  | param | notes |
  |---|---|
  | q | A ZIP **prefix**, or a substring of the market name. The ZIP half is anchored so the `{agencyId, zip5}` index can serve it. |
  | page / pageSize | 1-based; pageSize ≤ 200, default 50. Sorted by ZIP. |
  | agencyId | Which scope to list. Absent = the platform-global table, which is the only one anything writes in this ticket. |

  ## `agencyId: null` is a value, not an absence

  The table is platform-global: a campaign can serve many agencies, so during a
  preview no single agency owns the resolution. The column exists so per-agency
  overrides are additive later with no migration — the `Carrier` pattern, where
  `null` is stored explicitly so the query is unambiguous and the unique index
  has a real key to work with.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "page": 1, "pageSize": 25, "total": 2, "totalPages": 1,
    "items": [{
      "id": "…", "agencyId": null, "zip5": "99998",
      "market": "Bruno Test Market", "source": "manual",
      "updatedAt": "2026-09-06T…"
    }]
  }
  ```

  `source` says who decided: `seed` (the committed 564-row export), `preview`
  (an operator resolving an unmatched ZIP mid-campaign) or `manual` (this page).

  ## Errors
  - `401` / `403` — missing token, or missing `platform:mailers:read`.
}
